        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Qoder usage provider",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add a Qoder provider backed by the documented `big_model_credits` usage endpoint\n- support `qoder.com` and `qoder.com.cn` with Chrome cookie import, manual Cookie headers, and token-account overrides\n- handle documented and current response shapes, fractional/member/shared quotas, reset dates, cancellation, stale-cache retries, and regional fallback\n- register Qoder settings, CLI rendering, menu/widget behavior, icon resources, documentation, and regression coverage\n\nCloses #1590.\n\n## Live proof\n- the contributor verified an authenticated Qoder China account through Chrome cookies; the redacted run reported source `Chrome Default / qoder.com.cn` and `0 / 300 credits`\n- the attached screenshots are from that authenticated contributor run on an earlier head; exact head removes the duplicate generic Credits section visible there\n- an exact-head release CLI rerun completed browser import after Keychain authorization, but this maintainer environment had no authorized Qoder session in Chrome/config and correctly returned the missing-session error\n- both public Qoder usage endpoints were reachable and returned HTTP 401 without credentials; no cookie, auth header, token, account identity, or other secret is included here\n\n## Screenshots\nAuthenticated contributor run (pre-fix UI; exact head removes the second Credits section):\n\n<img width=\"1044\" height=\"1176\" alt=\"Qoder provider settings showing qoder.com.cn cookie source and 0 / 300 credits\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b56e63c1-d719-4b3c-9667-5c467dfc0c1b\" />\n\n<img width=\"622\" height=\"888\" alt=\"CodexBar menu showing Qoder tab with 100% left and 0 / 300 credits\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d2910929-72d4-4944-a083-ad05ba18afbb\" />\n\n## Validation\nExact head: `b78f420ca0f1a2147d2ed111ffa508b763bc4e06`\n\n- `swift test --filter Qoder` — 19 tests passed\n- `make check` — passed\n- `make test` — all 44 shards passed; one shard used the suite's clean built-in retry\n- `swift build -c release --product CodexBarCLI` — passed\n- bundled autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings\n- all 17 review threads answered and resolved\n",
